The function `gpiod_get_from_of_node()` now returns `ERR_PTR` when the "hpd-gpio" is not present in the device tree, but the original code did not handle this correctly. It assumed that an error would only occur if the return value was `NULL`, leading to incorrect error handling and potential crashes when the GPIO was not defined.

